Article 1 Anyone who, for the purpose of profit, produces, reproduces, publishes, sells, or disseminates obscene electronic information through the Internet or mobile communication terminals, shall be convicted and punished in accordance with Articles 1 and 2 of the Interpretation of the Supreme People's Court and the Supreme People's Procuratorate on Several Issues concerning the Specific Application of Law in Handling Criminal Cases of Producing, Reproducing, Publishing, Selling, and Disseminating Obscene Electronic Information through the Internet, Mobile Communication Terminals, and Voice Message Platforms.

Anyone who, for the purpose of profit, produces, reproduces, publishes, sells, or disseminates obscene electronic information containing minors under the age of fourteen through the Internet or mobile communication terminals, in any of the following circumstances, shall be convicted and punished for the crime of producing, reproducing, publishing, selling, or disseminating obscene articles for profit in accordance with paragraph 1 of Article 363 of the Criminal Law:
(1) producing, reproducing, publishing, selling, or disseminating ten or more video files such as obscene movies, performances, or animations;
(2) producing, reproducing, publishing, selling, or disseminating fifty or more obscene audio files;
(3) producing, reproducing, publishing, selling, or disseminating one hundred or more items of obscene electronic publications, pictures, or articles;
(4) the actual number of clicks on the obscene electronic information produced, reproduced, published, sold, or disseminated reaches 5,000 or more;
(5) publishing, selling, or disseminating obscene electronic information on a membership basis, with 100 or more registered members;
(6) using obscene electronic information to collect advertising fees, membership registration fees, or other fees, with illegal gains of 5,000 yuan or more;
(7) the quantity or amount, although not reaching the standards specified in items (1) to (6), respectively reaches more than half of the standards for two or more of those items;
(8) causing serious consequences.

Where a person commits the acts specified in paragraph 2, and the quantity or amount reaches five times or more the standards specified in items (1) to (7) of paragraph 2, it shall be deemed as "serious circumstances" as provided in paragraph 1 of Article 363 of the Criminal Law; where it reaches twenty-five times or more the specified standards, it shall be deemed as "particularly serious circumstances."

Article 2 Anyone who disseminates obscene electronic information through the Internet or mobile communication terminals shall be convicted and punished in accordance with Article 3 of the Interpretation of the Supreme People's Court and the Supreme People's Procuratorate on Several Issues concerning the Specific Application of Law in Handling Criminal Cases of Producing, Reproducing, Publishing, Selling, and Disseminating Obscene Electronic Information through the Internet, Mobile Communication Terminals, and Voice Message Platforms.

Anyone who disseminates obscene electronic information containing minors under the age of fourteen through the Internet or mobile communication terminals, in any of the following circumstances, shall be convicted and punished for the crime of disseminating obscene articles in accordance with paragraph 1 of Article 364 of the Criminal Law:
(1) the quantity reaches two times or more the standards specified in items (1) to (5) of paragraph 2 of Article 1;
(2) the quantity respectively reaches the standards for two or more of items (1) to (5) of paragraph 2 of Article 1;
(3) causing serious consequences.

Article 4 Where a website establisher or a directly responsible manager, for the purpose of profit, knowingly allows or tolerates another person to publish obscene electronic information on the website or webpage owned or managed by him/her, in any of the following circumstances, such person shall be convicted and punished for the crime of disseminating obscene articles for profit in accordance with paragraph 1 of Article 363 of the Criminal Law:
(1) the quantity or amount reaches five times or more the standards specified in items (1) to (6) of paragraph 2 of Article 1;
(2) the quantity or amount respectively reaches two times or more the standards for two or more of items (1) to (6) of paragraph 2 of Article 1;
(3) causing serious consequences.

Where a person commits the acts specified in the preceding paragraph, and the quantity or amount reaches twenty-five times or more the standards specified in items (1) to (7) of paragraph 2 of Article 1, it shall be deemed as "serious circumstances" as provided in paragraph 1 of Article 363 of the Criminal Law; where it reaches one hundred times or more the specified standards, it shall be deemed as "particularly serious circumstances."

Article 5 Where a website establisher or a directly responsible manager knowingly allows or tolerates another person to publish obscene electronic information on the website or webpage owned or managed by him/her, in any of the following circumstances, such person shall be convicted and punished for the crime of disseminating obscene articles in accordance with paragraph 1 of Article 364 of the Criminal Law:
(1) the quantity reaches ten times or more the standards specified in items (1) to (5) of paragraph 2 of Article 1;
(2) the quantity respectively reaches five times or more the standards for two or more of items (1) to (5) of paragraph 2 of Article 1;
(3) causing serious consequences.

Article 6 Where a telecommunications business operator or an Internet information service provider, knowing that a website is an obscene website, provides it with services such as Internet access, server hosting, network storage space, communication transmission channels, or fee collection on behalf of others, and collects service fees, in any of the following circumstances, the directly responsible supervisors and other directly liable persons shall be convicted and punished for the crime of disseminating obscene articles for profit in accordance with paragraph 1 of Article 363 of the Criminal Law:
(1) providing the above-mentioned services to five or more obscene websites;
(2) providing services such as Internet access, server hosting, network storage space, or communication transmission channels to an obscene website, with the amount of service fees collected reaching 20,000 yuan or more;
(3) providing fee collection services on behalf of an obscene website, with the amount of service fees collected reaching 50,000 yuan or more;
(4) causing serious consequences.

Where a person commits the acts specified in the preceding paragraph, and the quantity or amount reaches five times or more the standards specified in items (1) to (3) of the preceding paragraph, it shall be deemed as "serious circumstances" as provided in paragraph 1 of Article 363 of the Criminal Law; where it reaches twenty-five times or more the specified standards, it shall be deemed as "particularly serious circumstances."

Article 7 Where a person, knowing that a website is an obscene website and for the purpose of profit, directly or indirectly provides funds to it by placing advertisements or by other means, or provides fee settlement services, in any of the following circumstances, the directly responsible supervisors and other directly liable persons shall be punished as joint offenders of the crime of producing, reproducing, publishing, selling, or disseminating obscene articles for profit in accordance with paragraph 1 of Article 363 of the Criminal Law:
(1) placing advertisements or providing funds by other means to ten or more obscene websites;
(2) placing twenty or more advertisements on an obscene website;
(3) providing fee settlement services to ten or more obscene websites;
(4) providing funds to obscene websites by placing advertisements or by other means in an amount of 50,000 yuan or more;
(5) providing fee settlement services for an obscene website, with the amount of service fees collected reaching 20,000 yuan or more;
(6) causing serious consequences.

Where a person commits the acts specified in the preceding paragraph, and the quantity or amount reaches five times or more the standards specified in items (1) to (5) of the preceding paragraph, it shall be deemed as "serious circumstances" as provided in paragraph 1 of Article 363 of the Criminal Law; where it reaches twenty-five times or more the specified standards, it shall be deemed as "particularly serious circumstances."

Article 8 Where a person commits the acts specified in Articles 4 to 7, in any of the following circumstances, the person shall be determined to have "knowledge," unless there is evidence proving that he/she truly did not know:
(1) continuing to commit the above-mentioned acts after being notified in writing by the competent administrative authority;
(2) failing to perform statutory management duties after receiving a report;
(3) providing services such as Internet access, server hosting, network storage space, communication transmission channels, fee collection, or fee settlement to an obscene website, with the service fees collected being significantly higher than the market price;
(4) placing advertisements on an obscene website, where the advertisement click-through rate is significantly abnormal;
(5) other circumstances that can prove the person's knowledge.
